    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's helpful. My main concern is really the fear of losing items in the shuffle. When we have these massive amounts of loose papers and fragments that don't have clear headings, it feels almost like things are just disappearing into a void of disorder. Is there a specific metadata standard or workflow you'd recommend to prevent that kind of loss when dealing with such unpredictable and messy archival material?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
